{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"ffd4f239-62a6-4457-8f66-1e2bc3b1e6a9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 12, which defines “the State” for Fundamental Rights, appears in which Part of the Constitution?\",\"hi\":\"मौलिक अधिकारों के लिए “राज्य” को परिभाषित करने वाला अनुच्छेद 12 संविधान के किस भाग में है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Part III\",\"hi\":\"भाग III\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Part II\",\"hi\":\"भाग II\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Part IV\",\"hi\":\"भाग IV\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Part V\",\"hi\":\"भाग V\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 12, PDF page 37 (document page 7)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 12, PDF page 37 (document page 7)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 12, official PDF page 37 (document page 7)\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fe7e5276-e8ff-43fc-8db1-4caf7f0161c2\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A denominational public Hindu temple claims Article 26(b) to exclude an entire class of Hindus from worship. What did the Sri Venkataramana Devaru discussion support?\",\"hi\":\"एक सांप्रदायिक सार्वजनिक हिंदू मंदिर हिंदुओं के पूरे वर्ग को उपासना से बाहर रखने के लिए अनुच्छेद 26(b) का दावा करता है। श्री वेंकटरमण देवारू की विवेचना क्या समर्थन करती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 26(b) always defeats Article 25(2)(b)\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26(b) हमेशा अनुच्छेद 25(2)(b) पर प्रभावी होता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 26(b) is read subject to Article 25(2)(b) for temple entry, giving effect to both provisions harmoniously\",\"hi\":\"मंदिर-प्रवेश के लिए अनुच्छेद 26(b) को अनुच्छेद 25(2)(b) के अधीन पढ़ा जाता है, ताकि दोनों उपबंधों को सामंजस्यपूर्ण प्रभाव मिले\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 27 governs temple entry\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 27 मंदिर-प्रवेश नियंत्रित करता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 28(1) abolishes denominations\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 28(1) संप्रदायों को समाप्त करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=81 — Judgment, paragraphs 112-113, PDF page 81: individual and denominational rights; Article 26(b) read subject to Article 25(2)(b); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Aishat Shifa v. State of Karnataka, 2022 Supreme Court split decision (discussion of Sri Venkataramana Devaru)\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=81\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraphs 112-113, PDF page 81: individual and denominational rights; Article 26(b) read subject to Article 25(2)(b)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Aishat Shifa judgment discussing Sri Venkataramana Devaru, paragraphs 112-113, official Supreme Court PDF page 81; Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45; Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fcffd203-e4b0-4610-b548-61b9ed896dcd\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to NCERT, cultural-minority protection extends beyond religion to which identities?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT के अनुसार सांस्कृतिक अल्पसंख्यक-सुरक्षा धर्म से आगे किन पहचानों तक जाती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only occupational groups\",\"hi\":\"केवल व्यावसायिक समूह\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Linguistic and cultural minorities\",\"hi\":\"भाषायी और सांस्कृतिक अल्पसंख्यक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only political parties\",\"hi\":\"केवल राजनीतिक दल\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only taxpayers\",\"hi\":\"केवल करदाता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=15 — Printed page 40, PDF page 15: linguistic/cultural minorities, conservation, institutions and non-discrimination in aid\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=15\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 40, PDF page 15: linguistic/cultural minorities, conservation, institutions and non-discrimination in aid\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 40; Constitution of India, Articles 29 and 30(1), official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fca84a0a-46ff-482c-9523-18394f13f136\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Compulsory acquisition under Article 300A must ordinarily serve which purpose?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 300A के अधीन अनिवार्य अर्जन को सामान्यतः किस प्रयोजन की पूर्ति करनी चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A purely personal favour\",\"hi\":\"पूर्णतः निजी उपकार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A public purpose\",\"hi\":\"लोक प्रयोजन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"An undisclosed partisan goal\",\"hi\":\"अप्रकट दलीय लक्ष्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No identifiable purpose\",\"hi\":\"कोई पहचान योग्य प्रयोजन नहीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=45 — 2025 judgment, paragraph 41 quoting Kolkata Municipal Corporation, PDF page 45: notice, hearing, reasoned decision, public purpose and fair compensation\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"State of Himachal Pradesh v. Rajesh Chander Sood\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"2025 judgment, paragraph 41 quoting Kolkata Municipal Corporation, PDF page 45: notice, hearing, reasoned decision, public purpose and fair compensation\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Rajesh Chander Sood judgment, paragraph 41, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fc333e98-e678-4af9-803f-a6b6e57ba60f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A State-aided college compels every adult student to attend a religious ceremony despite written refusal. Which conclusion is strongest?\",\"hi\":\"एक राज्य-सहायता प्राप्त महाविद्यालय लिखित असहमति के बावजूद प्रत्येक वयस्क विद्यार्थी को धार्मिक समारोह में उपस्थित होने के लिए बाध्य करता है। सबसे मजबूत निष्कर्ष कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The compulsion is valid because aid removes all consent rights\",\"hi\":\"विवशता वैध है क्योंकि सहायता सभी सहमति-अधिकार समाप्त कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only Article 27 can apply\",\"hi\":\"केवल अनुच्छेद 27 लागू हो सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The compulsion conflicts with Article 28(3)\",\"hi\":\"विवशता अनुच्छेद 28(3) से असंगत है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The student must first be a minor\",\"hi\":\"विद्यार्थी का पहले अवयस्क होना आवश्यक है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fbe23b99-e762-4f14-b3cf-317c6b6f14a5\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does Article 13(4) say about a constitutional amendment made under Article 368?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 13(4), अनुच्छेद 368 के अधीन किए गए संविधान संशोधन के बारे में क्या कहता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It is automatically void\",\"hi\":\"वह स्वतः शून्य है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It requires approval by every court\",\"hi\":\"उसे प्रत्येक न्यायालय की स्वीकृति चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 13 does not apply to it\",\"hi\":\"उस पर अनुच्छेद 13 लागू नहीं होता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It becomes an ordinary rule\",\"hi\":\"वह साधारण नियम बन जाता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=260 — Part XX, Article 368(3), PDF page 260 (document page 229); Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=5 — Judgment, PDF pages 5-7: Shankari Prasad, Sajjan Singh, Golaknath, Twenty-fourth Amendment and Kesavananda Bharati\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=260\",\"citation\":\"Part XX, Article 368(3), PDF page 260 (document page 229)\"},{\"title\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, (2007) 2 SCC 1\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=5\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF pages 5-7: Shankari Prasad, Sajjan Singh, Golaknath, Twenty-fourth Amendment and Kesavananda Bharati\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 13(4) and 368(3), official PDF pages 37 and 260; I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, official Supreme Court PDF pages 5-7\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fbdd00ba-9bc4-49af-96b8-a31adf1de771\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How must property protected by Article 26(d) be administered?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26(d) से संरक्षित संपत्ति का प्रशासन कैसे किया जाना चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"In accordance with law\",\"hi\":\"विधि के अनुसार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Without any legal regulation\",\"hi\":\"किसी विधिक विनियमन के बिना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only by Parliament\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद द्वारा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only after a referendum\",\"hi\":\"केवल जनमत-संग्रह के बाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fabaf75e-0f61-4acf-866a-6add412a960f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A school is wholly State-funded, State-administered, and was established under a trust requiring religious instruction. Which combined reading of Article 28 is correct?\",\"hi\":\"एक विद्यालय पूर्णतः राज्य-पोषित और राज्य-प्रशासित है तथा ऐसे न्यास के अधीन स्थापित हुआ था जिसमें धार्मिक शिक्षा अपेक्षित है। अनुच्छेद 28 का कौन-सा संयुक्त पाठ सही है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Clause (1) applies without any exception and clause (3) is irrelevant\",\"hi\":\"खंड (1) बिना अपवाद लागू होता है और खंड (3) अप्रासंगिक है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Clause (2) permits compulsory worship for every minor\",\"hi\":\"खंड (2) प्रत्येक अवयस्क के लिए अनिवार्य उपासना की अनुमति देता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The trust automatically ends State administration\",\"hi\":\"न्यास स्वतः राज्य प्रशासन समाप्त कर देता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Clause (2) supplies the instruction exception, while clause (3) still protects consent against compelled participation in a recognised or aided institution\",\"hi\":\"खंड (2) धार्मिक शिक्षा का अपवाद देता है, जबकि खंड (3) मान्यताप्राप्त या सहायता-प्राप्त संस्था में विवश भागीदारी के विरुद्ध सहमति की रक्षा करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 26(b)-(d), 27 and 28, PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 26-28, official PDF page 46\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8e9dcd5-68d3-47e6-af6e-c137093b9023\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A prisoner seeks immediate release only because a remission request is pending, while custody rests on a valid sentence of a competent court. Which answer is most accurate?\",\"hi\":\"एक कैदी केवल इसलिए तत्काल मुक्ति चाहता है कि उसकी परिहार-अर्जी लंबित है, जबकि अभिरक्षा सक्षम न्यायालय के वैध दंडादेश पर आधारित है। सबसे सटीक उत्तर कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Habeas corpus automatically grants remission\",\"hi\":\"बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण स्वतः परिहार देता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Habeas corpus is not the ordinary means to replace lawful custody merely on that basis\",\"hi\":\"केवल उस आधार पर वैध अभिरक्षा को प्रतिस्थापित करने का बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण सामान्य साधन नहीं है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Quo warranto grants release\",\"hi\":\"अधिकार-पृच्छा मुक्ति देती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Prohibition annuls the conviction automatically\",\"hi\":\"प्रतिषेध दोषसिद्धि स्वतः समाप्त करती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/18046/18046_2019_11_1501_19778_Judgement_23-Jan-2020.pdf#page=10 — Judgment dated 23 January 2020, paragraphs 14-17, PDF page 10: lawful detention limitation and core inquiry; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/18046/18046_2019_11_1501_19778_Judgement_23-Jan-2020.pdf#page=16 — Judgment dated 23 January 2020, paragraphs 22-25, PDF page 16: procedural object and competent-court custody\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Home Secretary (Prison) v. H. Nilofer Nisha\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/18046/18046_2019_11_1501_19778_Judgement_23-Jan-2020.pdf#page=10\",\"citation\":\"Judgment dated 23 January 2020, paragraphs 14-17, PDF page 10: lawful detention limitation and core inquiry\"},{\"title\":\"The Home Secretary (Prison) v. H. Nilofer Nisha\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/18046/18046_2019_11_1501_19778_Judgement_23-Jan-2020.pdf#page=16\",\"citation\":\"Judgment dated 23 January 2020, paragraphs 22-25, PDF page 16: procedural object and competent-court custody\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"H. Nilofer Nisha judgment, paragraphs 14-17, official PDF page 10; H. Nilofer Nisha judgment, paragraphs 22-25, official PDF page 16\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8e70ef7-d4be-4d80-8976-87fc4ab66c0f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 300A is located in which Part of the Constitution?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 300A संविधान के किस भाग में स्थित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Part XII\",\"hi\":\"भाग XII\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Part III\",\"hi\":\"भाग III\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Part IV\",\"hi\":\"भाग IV\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Part IVA\",\"hi\":\"भाग IVA\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf#page=201 — Part XII, Chapter IV, Article 300A and Forty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 201 (document page 170)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf#page=201\",\"citation\":\"Part XII, Chapter IV, Article 300A and Forty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 201 (document page 170)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 300A and insertion footnote, official PDF page 201\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f86e061a-6d86-4c9f-b761-4369562e7232\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which two conditions form the classic Article 14 test of permissible classification?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 14 के अधीन अनुमेय वर्गीकरण की पारंपरिक कसौटी किन दो शर्तों से बनती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Intelligible differentia and a rational relation to the statutory object\",\"hi\":\"बोधगम्य विभेद और विधि के उद्देश्य से युक्तियुक्त संबंध\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Unanimous approval and retrospective operation\",\"hi\":\"सर्वसम्मत स्वीकृति और भूतलक्षी प्रवर्तन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Presidential order and judicial appointment\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति आदेश और न्यायिक नियुक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Religious identity and residence only\",\"hi\":\"केवल धार्मिक पहचान और निवास\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/864.pdf#page=3 — Judgment, PDF page 3: Article 14 permits reasonable classification subject to intelligible differentia and rational nexus\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Budhan Choudhry v. State of Bihar, 1955 1 SCR 1045\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/864.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF page 3: Article 14 permits reasonable classification subject to intelligible differentia and rational nexus\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Budhan Choudhry v. State of Bihar, official Supreme Court PDF page 3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f86b6445-c826-4ca2-98c7-bf42f64164df\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which sequence best states the I.R. Coelho test for a post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule law?\",\"hi\":\"24 अप्रैल 1973 के बाद नौवीं अनुसूची में रखी विधि के लिए आई.आर. कोएल्हो की कसौटी का सही क्रम क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Check only whether Parliament used the word “amendment”\",\"hi\":\"केवल जाँचें कि संसद ने “संशोधन” शब्द प्रयोग किया\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Assume automatic immunity and end review\",\"hi\":\"स्वतः उन्मुक्ति मानकर जाँच समाप्त करें\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Review only the law’s title\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधि का शीर्षक जाँचें\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"First identify Part III infringement, then assess its impact on basic structure; invalidate if the impact destroys or damages basic structure\",\"hi\":\"पहले भाग III के उल्लंघन को पहचानें, फिर मूल संरचना पर उसके प्रभाव की जाँच करें; प्रभाव मूल संरचना को नष्ट या क्षतिग्रस्त करे तो अमान्य ठहराएँ\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=40 — Conclusion, PDF pages 40-41: post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule amendments, rights/impact test and basic-structure review\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, (2007) 2 SCC 1\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/28469.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Conclusion, PDF pages 40-41: post-24 April 1973 Ninth Schedule amendments, rights/impact test and basic-structure review\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"I.R. Coelho v. State of Tamil Nadu, conclusion, official Supreme Court PDF pages 40-41\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f78d17d6-9bb2-4b46-8957-a67fcaef9256\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Students respectfully stand during the National Anthem but decline to sing because of a sincere religious belief. Which precedent was cited as upholding their protection?\",\"hi\":\"विद्यार्थी राष्ट्रगान के समय सम्मानपूर्वक खड़े रहते हैं, पर सच्चे धार्मिक विश्वास के कारण गाने से इनकार करते हैं। उनकी सुरक्षा को मान्यता देने वाले किस पूर्वनिर्णय का उल्लेख किया गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Rev. Stainislaus\",\"hi\":\"रेव. स्टेनिस्लॉस\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Bijoe Emmanuel v. State of Kerala\",\"hi\":\"बिजो इमैनुएल बनाम केरल राज्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Sri Venkataramana Devaru\",\"hi\":\"श्री वेंकटरमण देवारू\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A tax-appropriation case under Article 27\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 27 का कर-विनियोग वाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=86 — Judgment, paragraph 116, PDF page 86: students stood respectfully but did not sing the National Anthem; Article 25 protection discussed; Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Aishat Shifa v. State of Karnataka, 2022 Supreme Court split decision (discussion of Bijoe Emmanuel)\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/8344/8344_2022_6_1501_38867_Judgement_13-Oct-2022.pdf#page=86\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraph 116, PDF page 86: students stood respectfully but did not sing the National Anthem; Article 25 protection discussed\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Aishat Shifa judgment discussing Bijoe Emmanuel, paragraph 116, official Supreme Court PDF page 86; Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f75c71c3-79ea-441c-b75c-468b4c26ad3a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which personal interest has been recognised under Article 21 alongside privacy and dignity?\",\"hi\":\"निजता और गरिमा के साथ किस व्यक्तिगत हित को अनुच्छेद 21 के अधीन मान्यता मिली है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Reputation\",\"hi\":\"प्रतिष्ठा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary title\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत उपाधि\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Tax immunity\",\"hi\":\"कर उन्मुक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A right to defame others\",\"hi\":\"दूसरों को बदनाम करने का अधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=428 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 65 footnote, PDF page 428: judicially recognised Article 21 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=428\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 65 footnote, PDF page 428: judicially recognised Article 21 protections\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraph 65 footnote, official PDF page 428\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f7271adc-c608-472c-aad2-7aeaba21262d\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 21A expressly covers children in which age group?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21A स्पष्टतः किस आयु-वर्ग के बच्चों को आच्छादित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Three to six years\",\"hi\":\"तीन से छह वर्ष\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Six to fourteen years\",\"hi\":\"छह से चौदह वर्ष\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Fourteen to eighteen years\",\"hi\":\"चौदह से अठारह वर्ष\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Eighteen to twenty-one years\",\"hi\":\"अठारह से इक्कीस वर्ष\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42 — Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6 — Printed page 31, PDF page 6: Right to Freedom overview and Articles 19-22 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 31, PDF page 6: Right to Freedom overview and Articles 19-22 protections\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), official PDF page 42; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 31\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f671fb6a-6bac-401e-803b-bf60fc717e55\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does section 7 do to a bonded labourer’s property encumbered in connection with bonded debt?\",\"hi\":\"बंधित ऋण से संबंधित भार वाली बंधित श्रमिक की संपत्ति के लिए धारा 7 क्या करती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Frees it from the related mortgage, charge, lien or other encumbrance\",\"hi\":\"उसे संबंधित बंधक, भार, धारणाधिकार या अन्य विल्लंगम से मुक्त करती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Transfers it permanently to the creditor\",\"hi\":\"उसे स्थायी रूप से लेनदार को देती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Requires its destruction\",\"hi\":\"उसका विनाश अपेक्षित करती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Converts it into public property\",\"hi\":\"उसे सार्वजनिक संपत्ति बनाती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=5 — Sections 7-12, PDF page 5: property, homestead and District Magistrate duties\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976 (Act 19 of 1976)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=5\",\"citation\":\"Sections 7-12, PDF page 5: property, homestead and District Magistrate duties\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976, sections 7-12, official India Code PDF page 5\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f63d9e04-16a4-4446-8a7a-b6baea8e2f0f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which clause of Article 26 protects establishing and maintaining religious and charitable institutions?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 26 का कौन-सा खंड धार्मिक और पूर्त संस्थाओं की स्थापना और पोषण की रक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Clause (d)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (d)\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Clause (a)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (a)\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Clause (c)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (c)\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Clause (b)\",\"hi\":\"खंड (b)\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5bedb28-c6c7-4457-9bc5-fb2ddcc861cc\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A visitor who is not an Indian citizen asks whether the beneficiary wording of Articles 19 and 21 is identical. Which answer follows from the text?\",\"hi\":\"एक ऐसा आगंतुक जो भारतीय नागरिक नहीं है पूछता है कि क्या अनुच्छेद 19 और 21 की लाभार्थी-भाषा समान है। पाठ से कौन-सा उत्तर निकलता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No; Article 19 is framed for citizens, while Article 21 protects any person\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; अनुच्छेद 19 नागरिकों के लिए है, जबकि अनुच्छेद 21 किसी भी व्यक्ति की रक्षा करता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Yes; both apply only to citizens by birth\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; दोनों केवल जन्मजात नागरिकों पर लागू होते हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Yes; both protect only elected representatives\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; दोनों केवल निर्वाचित प्रतिनिधियों की रक्षा करते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No; Article 19 protects only non-citizens\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; अनुच्छेद 19 केवल गैर-नागरिकों की रक्षा करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), PDF page 40 (document page 9); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42 — Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=9 — Printed page 34, PDF page 9: meaning of liberty, Article 21 and arrest safeguards\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=9\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 34, PDF page 9: meaning of liberty, Article 21 and arrest safeguards\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), official PDF page 40; Constitution of India, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), official PDF page 42; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 34\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5237f06-d1be-47a5-b485-36c365286681\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the immediate effect of section 4(1) of the Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act?\",\"hi\":\"बंधित श्रम पद्धति (उत्सादन) अधिनियम की धारा 4(1) का तात्कालिक प्रभाव क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It creates a new bonded debt\",\"hi\":\"यह नया बंधित ऋण बनाती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It abolishes the system and frees bonded labourers from the obligation to render bonded labour\",\"hi\":\"यह पद्धति समाप्त कर बंधित श्रमिकों को बंधित श्रम देने के दायित्व से मुक्त करती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It permits forced labour by contract\",\"hi\":\"यह संविदा से बलात् श्रम अनुमति देती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It applies only to future courts\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल भावी न्यायालयों पर लागू होती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=3 — Sections 2-4, PDF page 3: definitions, overriding effect and abolition of bonded labour system\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976 (Act 19 of 1976)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Sections 2-4, PDF page 3: definitions, overriding effect and abolition of bonded labour system\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976, sections 2-4, official India Code PDF page 3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f4278599-b8b0-40ec-905e-ce7c8197170e\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why did Joseph Shine find Section 497 inconsistent with substantive equality?\",\"hi\":\"जोसेफ शाइन ने धारा 497 को तात्त्विक समानता से असंगत क्यों पाया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It applied only to taxation\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल कराधान पर लागू थी\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It perpetuated women’s subordinate status and gender stereotypes within marriage\",\"hi\":\"इसने विवाह में महिलाओं की अधीनस्थ स्थिति और लैंगिक रूढ़ियों को बनाए रखा\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It required equal punishment for all spouses\",\"hi\":\"इसने सभी जीवनसाथियों के लिए समान दंड चाहा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It protected sexual autonomy\",\"hi\":\"इसने यौन स्वायत्तता की रक्षा की\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/32550/32550_2017_Judgement_27-Sep-2018.pdf#page=180 — Constitution Bench judgment, conclusions 1-4, PDF page 180: Section 497, equality, stereotypes, dignity, liberty, privacy and autonomy\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Joseph Shine v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/32550/32550_2017_Judgement_27-Sep-2018.pdf#page=180\",\"citation\":\"Constitution Bench judgment, conclusions 1-4, PDF page 180: Section 497, equality, stereotypes, dignity, liberty, privacy and autonomy\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Joseph Shine judgment, conclusions 1-4, official PDF page 180\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f4187a8b-cf06-47d9-9120-e28668298b56\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 15(2)(b) covers the use of which facilities when maintained from State funds or dedicated to public use?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 15(2)(b) राज्य निधि से पोषित या सार्वजनिक उपयोग के लिए समर्पित किन सुविधाओं के उपयोग को आच्छादित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only private bedrooms\",\"hi\":\"केवल निजी शयनकक्ष\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only legislative chambers\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधायी सदन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only foreign embassies\",\"hi\":\"केवल विदेशी दूतावास\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Wells, tanks, bathing ghats, roads and places of public resort\",\"hi\":\"कुएँ, तालाब, स्नानघाट, सड़कें और सार्वजनिक समागम-स्थान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=38 — Part III, Article 15(2)-(6) and amendment footnotes, PDF page 38 (document page 7); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6 — Printed pages 31-33, PDF pages 6-8: Right to Equality, equal access, reservation, untouchability and titles\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=38\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 15(2)-(6) and amendment footnotes, PDF page 38 (document page 7)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6\",\"citation\":\"Printed pages 31-33, PDF pages 6-8: Right to Equality, equal access, reservation, untouchability and titles\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 15(2)-(6), official PDF page 38; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed pages 31-33\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f2fae112-94d5-453d-acd8-aa5e0c5764cf\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which condition is essential before a custom or usage is treated as “law” under Article 13(3)(a)?\",\"hi\":\"किस शर्त के पूरा होने पर रूढ़ि या प्रथा को अनुच्छेद 13(3)(a) के अधीन “विधि” माना जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It must be written in English\",\"hi\":\"उसे अंग्रेज़ी में लिखा होना चाहिए\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It must be older than one hundred years\",\"hi\":\"वह सौ वर्ष से पुरानी होनी चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It must be approved by every State Legislature\",\"hi\":\"उसे हर राज्य विधानमंडल की स्वीकृति होनी चाहिए\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It must have the force of law in the territory of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत के राज्यक्षेत्र में उसे विधि का बल प्राप्त होना चाहिए\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37 — Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=37\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 13 and Twenty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 37 (document page 6)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 13, official PDF page 37\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f237a17a-c7bc-44e0-9a37-4e767f978c3d\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does Article 16(5) protect from being invalidated by Article 16?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 16(5) किस व्यवस्था को अनुच्छेद 16 के कारण अमान्य होने से बचाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary political titles\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत राजनीतिक उपाधियाँ\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Discrimination in every private job\",\"hi\":\"हर निजी नौकरी में भेदभाव\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"All residence requirements made by executives\",\"hi\":\"कार्यपालिका द्वारा बनाई सभी निवास अपेक्षाएँ\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A law requiring an office connected with a religious or denominational institution to be held by a person professing that religion or denomination\",\"hi\":\"धार्मिक या सांप्रदायिक संस्था से जुड़े पद को उस धर्म या संप्रदाय को मानने वाले व्यक्ति द्वारा धारण करने की अपेक्षा वाली विधि\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, official PDF page 40\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f16bfee9-3ceb-45bc-9758-e2f57960d992\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"In Ajay Hasia, why was the Regional Engineering College society held to be an “authority” under Article 12?\",\"hi\":\"अजय हसिया में क्षेत्रीय इंजीनियरिंग महाविद्यालय की सोसाइटी को अनुच्छेद 12 के अधीन “प्राधिकारी” क्यों माना गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The established facts showed deep governmental financing, control, direction and dominance over its governing structure\",\"hi\":\"स्थापित तथ्यों से उसके शासी ढाँचे पर गहन सरकारी वित्तपोषण, नियंत्रण, निर्देशन और प्रभुत्व सिद्ध हुआ\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every educational institution is automatically State\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक शैक्षणिक संस्था स्वतः राज्य है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It was located in a capital city\",\"hi\":\"वह राजधानी में स्थित थी\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Its students received degrees\",\"hi\":\"उसके विद्यार्थियों को उपाधियाँ मिलती थीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/4414.pdf#page=19 — Judgment, PDF page 19: application of the test to the Regional Engineering College society\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Ajay Hasia v. Khalid Mujib Sehravardi, (1981) 1 SCC 722\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/4414.pdf#page=19\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, PDF page 19: application of the test to the Regional Engineering College society\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Ajay Hasia v. Khalid Mujib Sehravardi, official Supreme Court PDF page 19\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f1155b81-89fd-448e-9a3d-69876345b566\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How does the Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 define “civil rights”?\",\"hi\":\"सिविल अधिकार संरक्षण अधिनियम, 1955 “सिविल अधिकार” को कैसे परिभाषित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Any contractual right\",\"hi\":\"कोई भी संविदात्मक अधिकार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only voting rights\",\"hi\":\"केवल मतदान अधिकार\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A right accruing to a person by reason of the abolition of untouchability by Article 17\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 17 द्वारा अस्पृश्यता के अंत के कारण किसी व्यक्ति को प्राप्त अधिकार\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only property rights\",\"hi\":\"केवल संपत्ति अधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/15434/1/protection_of_civil_rights_act%2C_1955.pdf#page=2 — Long title and Sections 1-2, PDF page 2: punishment for untouchability disabilities and definition of civil rights by reference to Article 17; Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955 (Act 22 of 1955)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/15434/1/protection_of_civil_rights_act%2C_1955.pdf#page=2\",\"citation\":\"Long title and Sections 1-2, PDF page 2: punishment for untouchability disabilities and definition of civil rights by reference to Article 17\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Protection of Civil Rights Act, 1955, Sections 1-2, official India Code PDF page 2; Constitution of India, Articles 16(5)-(6), 17 and 18, official PDF page 40\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f0e1aca8-f627-497f-9a67-02dd65526352\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What kind of proceedings does Article 32(1) contemplate for moving the Supreme Court?\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय जाने के लिए अनुच्छेद 32(1) किस प्रकार की कार्यवाही का विचार करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only a criminal appeal\",\"hi\":\"केवल दांडिक अपील\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only a presidential reference\",\"hi\":\"केवल राष्ट्रपति का निर्देश\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only a civil suit\",\"hi\":\"केवल दीवानी वाद\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Appropriate proceedings\",\"hi\":\"समुचित कार्यवाही\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=50 — Part III, Article 32(1)-(4), PDF page 50 (document page 19)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=50\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 32(1)-(4), PDF page 50 (document page 19)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 32(1)-(4), official PDF page 50\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f05a9e5e-72bd-4e7c-a424-198550767fa8\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"When a private contractor violates Article 23, what constitutional responsibility did the PUDR discussion place on the State?\",\"hi\":\"जब निजी ठेकेदार अनुच्छेद 23 का उल्लंघन करे, PUDR की विवेचना ने राज्य पर कौन-सी संवैधानिक जिम्मेदारी रखी?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"To ignore every private violation\",\"hi\":\"हर निजी उल्लंघन की उपेक्षा करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"To take necessary steps to stop the violation and ensure observance of the right\",\"hi\":\"उल्लंघन रोकने और अधिकार का पालन सुनिश्चित करने हेतु आवश्यक कदम उठाना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"To convert the contractor into a court\",\"hi\":\"ठेकेदार को न्यायालय में बदलना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"To suspend Article 23\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 23 निलंबित करना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/51059/51059_2023_1_1502_56228_Judgement_03-Oct-2024.pdf#page=50 — Judgment, paragraph 74, PDF page 50: PUDR holding on minimum wage, Article 23 and State duty against private violations; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2016/27156/27156_2016_3_1501_40744_Judgement_03-Jan-2023.pdf#page=14 — Judgment, Question No. 2 discussion, PDF page 14: Articles 23 and 24 enforceable against private citizens\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Property Owners Association v. State of Maharashtra, 2024 INSC 753\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/51059/51059_2023_1_1502_56228_Judgement_03-Oct-2024.pdf#page=50\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraph 74, PDF page 50: PUDR holding on minimum wage, Article 23 and State duty against private violations\"},{\"title\":\"Kaushal Kishor v. State of Uttar Pradesh, 2023 INSC 4\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2016/27156/27156_2016_3_1501_40744_Judgement_03-Jan-2023.pdf#page=14\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, Question No. 2 discussion, PDF page 14: Articles 23 and 24 enforceable against private citizens\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Property Owners Association judgment, paragraph 74 discussing PUDR, official Supreme Court PDF page 50; Kaushal Kishor judgment, Question No. 2 discussion, official Supreme Court PDF page 14\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f01469b7-333f-4b76-bf25-e6ba5605b4fe\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What precondition must exist before the President can make an order under Article 359(1)?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 359(1) के अधीन राष्ट्रपति के आदेश से पहले कौन-सी पूर्वशर्त विद्यमान होनी चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A financial bill must fail\",\"hi\":\"वित्त विधेयक विफल होना चाहिए\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A Proclamation of Emergency must be in operation\",\"hi\":\"आपातकाल की उद्घोषणा प्रवर्तन में होनी चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Every High Court must consent\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक उच्च न्यायालय की सहमति होनी चाहिए\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A State election must be pending\",\"hi\":\"राज्य निर्वाचन लंबित होना चाहिए\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=247 — Part XVIII, Article 359(1)-(1A) and amendment footnote, PDF page 247 (document page 216)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=247\",\"citation\":\"Part XVIII, Article 359(1)-(1A) and amendment footnote, PDF page 247 (document page 216)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 359(1)-(1A), official PDF page 247\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f00dfb5c-2d0e-4027-80d3-a24b13f9b115\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Who is equally entitled under Article 25(1) to freedom of conscience and the specified religious freedoms?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 25(1) के अधीन अंतःकरण और निर्दिष्ट धार्मिक स्वतंत्रताओं का समान अधिकार किसे है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Citizens only\",\"hi\":\"केवल नागरिकों को\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"All persons\",\"hi\":\"सभी व्यक्तियों को\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Religious denominations only\",\"hi\":\"केवल धार्मिक संप्रदायों को\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Public officials only\",\"hi\":\"केवल लोक अधिकारियों को\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45 — Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, PDF page 45 (document page 14)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 25 and Article 26 opening, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"efb74968-cd72-47fc-8574-05ec5f86fb25\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the statements: 1. Article 29(1) protects a qualifying section of citizens. 2. Article 30 covers religious and linguistic minorities. 3. Educational-standard regulation may be valid if it preserves minority character. Which are correct?\",\"hi\":\"कथनों पर विचार कीजिए: 1. अनुच्छेद 29(1) नागरिकों के अर्ह अनुभाग की रक्षा करता है। 2. अनुच्छेद 30 धार्मिक और भाषायी अल्पसंख्यकों को आच्छादित करता है। 3. शैक्षणिक मानक-विनियमन अल्पसंख्यक स्वरूप सुरक्षित रखने पर वैध हो सकता है। कौन-से सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 and 2 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 2\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46 — Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=47 — Part III, Article 30(1A)-(2) and amendment footnote, PDF page 47 (document page 16); Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2024/14432/14432_2024_1_1502_56834_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=42 — Judgment, paragraphs 57-59, PDF page 42: permissible regulation of educational standards; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2024/14432/14432_2024_1_1502_56834_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=43 — Judgment, paragraphs 59-61, PDF page 43: recognition conditions and preservation of minority status\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 29 and 30(1), PDF page 46 (document page 15)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=47\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 30(1A)-(2) and amendment footnote, PDF page 47 (document page 16)\"},{\"title\":\"Anjum Kadari v. Union of India, 2024 INSC 831\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2024/14432/14432_2024_1_1502_56834_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=42\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraphs 57-59, PDF page 42: permissible regulation of educational standards\"},{\"title\":\"Anjum Kadari v. Union of India, 2024 INSC 831\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2024/14432/14432_2024_1_1502_56834_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=43\",\"citation\":\"Judgment, paragraphs 59-61, PDF page 43: recognition conditions and preservation of minority status\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 29 and 30(1), official PDF page 46; Constitution of India, Article 30(1A)-(2), official PDF page 47; Anjum Kadari judgment, paragraphs 57-59, official Supreme Court PDF page 42; Anjum Kadari judgment, paragraphs 59-61, official Supreme Court PDF page 43\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ef9fa1a2-8c65-4ad9-a734-3ac37cb99bf1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A municipality removes the only means by which a group earns its livelihood, without lawful authority or a fair procedure. Which Article 21 principle is most relevant?\",\"hi\":\"नगरपालिका किसी समूह के जीवन-निर्वाह के एकमात्र साधन को बिना विधिक प्राधिकार या न्यायसंगत प्रक्रिया के हटा देती है। अनुच्छेद 21 का कौन-सा सिद्धांत सर्वाधिक प्रासंगिक है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every occupation is unregulatable\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक व्यवसाय अविनियमनीय है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The group owns all public land\",\"hi\":\"समूह समस्त सार्वजनिक भूमि का स्वामी है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Livelihood is an incident of life, so deprivation requires lawful and fair treatment\",\"hi\":\"आजीविका जीवन का आनुषंगिक अंग है, अतः वंचन विधिसम्मत और न्यायसंगत होना चाहिए\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 21 concerns elections only\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21 केवल चुनावों से संबंधित है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=110 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraphs 113-114, PDF page 110: dignified existence and livelihood as an incident of life; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=210 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 150, PDF page 210: fair and reasonable procedure and Article 21 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=110\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraphs 113-114, PDF page 110: dignified existence and livelihood as an incident of life\"},{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=210\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 150, PDF page 210: fair and reasonable procedure and Article 21 protections\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraphs 113-114, official PDF page 110; K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraph 150, official PDF page 210\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee7b2ebb-3520-491a-9d1f-4682775fdf3e\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the status under section 5 of a custom or contract requiring bonded labour?\",\"hi\":\"धारा 5 के अधीन बंधित श्रम अपेक्षित करने वाली रूढ़ि या संविदा की स्थिति क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Permanently enforceable\",\"hi\":\"स्थायी रूप से प्रवर्तनीय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Valid only if oral\",\"hi\":\"केवल मौखिक होने पर वैध\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Void and inoperative\",\"hi\":\"शून्य और अप्रवर्तनीय\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Automatically converted into tax\",\"hi\":\"स्वतः कर में परिवर्तित\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India — https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=4 — Sections 5-6, PDF page 4: void agreements and extinguishment of bonded debt\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976 (Act 19 of 1976)\",\"institution\":\"India Code, Legislative Department, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/1491/1/197619.pdf#page=4\",\"citation\":\"Sections 5-6, PDF page 4: void agreements and extinguishment of bonded debt\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Bonded Labour System (Abolition) Act, 1976, sections 5-6, official India Code PDF page 4\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ede08017-0df0-4d04-a8a7-a7a48884fbd7\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why is Article 30 administration not treated as absolute by the Supreme Court?\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय अनुच्छेद 30 के प्रशासन को निरपेक्ष क्यों नहीं मानता?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Because Article 30 was repealed\",\"hi\":\"क्योंकि अनुच्छेद 30 निरसित हो गया\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Because administration carries a duty to provide standards and does not protect maladministration\",\"hi\":\"क्योंकि प्रशासन के साथ मानक देने का कर्तव्य जुड़ा है और कुप्रशासन संरक्षित नहीं है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Because only Parliament can run schools\",\"hi\":\"क्योंकि केवल संसद विद्यालय चला सकती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Because minorities cannot own assets\",\"hi\":\"क्योंकि अल्पसंख्यक परिसंपत्ति नहीं रख सकते\"}},\"difficu